{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400622-why-the-war-between-tzimisce-and-shadow-lord-lasted-so-long","id":1400622,"title":"Why the war between Tzimisce and Shadow Lord lasted so long?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-02T20:37:06-07:00","id":1400622,"title":"Why the war between Tzimisce and Shadow Lord lasted so long?","content":"<div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I have looked through Tzimisce Revised book and Transylvania by Night<span style=\"font-family:Helvetica,Arial,Verdana,sans-serif\">. </span></span></span></span>They have fought against each other since prehistoric time. But both sides have their own ultimate weapons</div> <br /> <br /> Tzimisces have horrible the Eldest and elders, Kupala is also included, of course<br /> Shadow Lords have pacts with powerful spirits, they can gain mystical legendary powers. And remember, they binded Kupapa firstly and created Carpathians and the Alps to last this restrain<br /> It is, well, very strange that one side didn't do something really badass to crush down the other...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 07-02-2020, 11:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T20:38:26-07:00","id":1400624,"title":"","content":"I want to see a detailed war between vampires and garou, like Underworld, but Under a Blood Red Moon is... lacking","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T22:21:44-07:00","id":1400634,"title":"","content":"Honest answer: lazy writing. They\u2019re associated with the same part of the world, so of course they must have been at war for all time. Except that\u2019s not actually how anything works, and depicting eastern people as unchanging and backwards and easily stereotyped is a known problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T22:50:44-07:00","id":1400637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400622-why-the-war-between-tzimisce-and-shadow-lord-lasted-so-long?p=1400634#post1400634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honest answer: lazy writing. They\u2019re associated with the same part of the world, so of course they must have been at war for all time. Except that\u2019s not actually how anything works, and depicting eastern people as unchanging and backwards and easily stereotyped is a known problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure I entirely agree. Impossibly long conflicts are a standard trope in fantasy writing and this likely comes to make the conflict seem more important and why a peaceful resolution don't come off as possible.<br /> <br /> Besides, there have been examples of really long conflicts in human history as well. The Greco-Roman conflict with the Zoroastrian civilization for instance. And given the, to my understanding, both relative isolation from each other due to the small numbers involved, both sides having a supernatural abilites to detect and escape from the other, and impossibility to fully commit against the other due to many other fronts to fight on this conflicts does not seem entirely impossible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T23:35:43-07:00","id":1400646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400622-why-the-war-between-tzimisce-and-shadow-lord-lasted-so-long?p=1400637#post1400637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides, there have been examples of really long conflicts in human history as well. The Greco-Roman conflict with the Zoroastrian civilization for instance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tzimisce and Shadow Lord have fought each other since the First City period if you refer to Tzimisce Revised book, Shadow Lord themselves say they have fought vampires since they had memories (Ironically, Tzimisce book has more details about the history of these wars, Shadow Lord is little instead)<br /> <br /> Not \u201cmerely\u201d hundreds or thousands of years<br /> <br /> And, to be honest, I think the very long history will birth some truly epic or famous wars which must be much greater than Chicago War, powerful entities involved or killed. But in Transylvania by Night they simple said some words to flit it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 07-03-2020, 02:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T23:51:02-07:00","id":1400650,"title":"","content":"My answer would be that vampires and garou both hold long grudges.<br /> <br /> The Tzimisce are immortal, hand down traditions, and view themselves as the rightful and absolute overlords of their lands. They would have no patience for competition and would carry grudges for centuries if not millennia once slighted. Just ask the Tremere or the Ventrue.<br /> <br /> The Shadow Lords are a tribe of garou, who are tradition by nature with strong oral histories and able to literally access their ancestors. Simultaneously they see themselves as divine champions on a religious crusade against creatures of corruption, including vampires, and the eventual pact with Kupala by Tzimisce fiends would not help matters.<br /> <br /> Given their natures it's almost inevitable there would have been a conflict. From then on it's centuries of back and forth guerrilla warfare. Tzimisce pledge to uphold the honor of their lineage and destroy Shadow Lords. Shadow Lords swear to avenge their ancestors and destroy packs of Tzimisce. The battle continues nigh on eternally, with the occasional pragmatic armistice to break things up.<br /> <br /> Hey they might both be ruthless, vicious, and willing to hold a grudge until they're last moment on earth; but some times you've just got other priorities.<br /> <br /> Like peasant uprisings. Or famines. Or Mongols.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T00:01:39-07:00","id":1400653,"title":"","content":"And this kind of long long war has a common point: they rarely strike the very core of both sides<br /> <br /> We never hear of any really powerful, named elders were killed by lupines. Velya, Yoark, and so on. These 4th and 5th gen elders are still around (or killed by others, not lupines at least). Needless to say Eldest himself (In fact in the whole WoD we never hear of any named methseulah are killed by lupines). Maybe they slaughtered a lot but we didn't know<br /> Of course no named <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">legendary or elder </span></span></span>Shadow Lords were killed by vampires, too. Tzimisce didn't really eliminate them<br /> <br /> From this perspective, history of Set seems to be more suitable, he made all supernaturals of Egypt suck very, very hard thousands of years ago, letting Silent Striders leave home, ghouling all Kinfolk of Bubasti, etc. And they all happened after hunderds of years' war<br /> Set is much younger than Tzimisce, well","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 07-03-2020, 03:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T00:07:11-07:00","id":1400654,"title":"","content":"I think the issue is probably just a matter of page count. Neither tribe or clan books really had the page count to devote to the nuances of a multi-millennia war that could have been a book in its own right. I do agree though that perhaps a few more pages with notable persons and events would have been nice, but then again, for every extra page that went to that we would have lost one from something else.<br /> <br /> So for me this becomes the territory of headcanon and the Storyteller's Vault.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T00:31:08-07:00","id":1400657,"title":"","content":"Its pretty silly. Surely all old wolves should have warred with all vampires? I'm under the assumption that the Shadow lords usually lost, and fighting was infrequent. <br /> <br /> As pointed out, Set's conflict is dope though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T00:54:10-07:00","id":1400658,"title":"","content":"I would think the general depiction of the war is actually one of prolonged, but sporadic conflicts that flare up from time to time, but with long periods of peace in between. During those flare ups, the Shadow Lords slaughter the vampire neonates, the vampire elders hide, and the Shadow Lords proclaim victory and go home, and the surviving vampire elders get even more powerful.<br /> <br /> For the Shadow Lords, victory is killing lots and lots of vampires. And they probably do kill a lot of neonates and some ancilla. For the vampire elders, victory is accomplishing whatever end goal they want regardless of the destruction of all those inferior neonates and ancillae. So both sides declare victory a lot. Since there is no objective perspective, it's hard to say who truly &quot;won&quot;.<br /> <br /> I think every now and then, the Shadow Lords gain a decisive victory in that they actually kill some elder vampire. Likewise there are some conflicts where the casualties among the Shadow Lords are too excessive for the number of vampires they kill.<br /> <br /> Overall, who is ahead depends on what you want the current status quo to be compared to what it was. Since the Tzimisce really got hurt bad during the Anarch Revolt, and many members fled to the New World, the Shadow Lords have probably marginally come out on top for reasons independent of their own actions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T00:55:49-07:00","id":1400659,"title":"","content":"I just told a phenonmenon<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400622-why-the-war-between-tzimisce-and-shadow-lord-lasted-so-long?p=1400657#post1400657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Its pretty silly. Surely all old wolves should have warred with all vampires? </span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> I never expressed meanings like this</span></span></span></div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400622-why-the-war-between-tzimisce-and-shadow-lord-lasted-so-long?p=1400657#post1400657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">As pointed out, Set's conflict is dope though.</span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> Mind you, the reason why I say Set's history makes sense is that it had a result relatively quickly, not after an eternal war, then nearly nonthing very noted happened. And one side may be crushed down hard<br /> <br /> His conflict itself is dope, true</span></span></span></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T03:09:12-07:00","id":1400673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Flag</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400622-why-the-war-between-tzimisce-and-shadow-lord-lasted-so-long?p=1400634#post1400634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honest answer: lazy writing. They\u2019re associated with the same part of the world, so of course they must have been at war for all time. Except that\u2019s not actually how anything works, and depicting eastern people as unchanging and backwards and easily stereotyped is a known problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternatively: Shadow Lords are heroic and passionately committed warriors against an intractable evil enemy.<br /> <br /> My take on the Shadow Lords have always been that they get stereotyped by the Silver Fangs (who are Russian so it's Western versus Eastern nobility) as being greedy and duplicitous but they have been shaped by a personal conflcit against the Tzimisce that has lasted thousands of years. The Tzimisce are too powerful, intelligent, and dangerous to defeat but the Shadow Lords never give up either so it is a war that goes on and on forever. At least until the Tremere appear and the tide finally turns against the Tzimisce.<br /> <br /> The source of the war, FYI, is the fact the Tzimisce are connected to the Shadow Lord's archenemy Kupala and are the original group that gathered mortal resources and wealth to fight against the Garou.<br /> <br /> I.e. they're the original Pentex.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 07-03-2020, 06:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T05:30:44-07:00","id":1400705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400622-why-the-war-between-tzimisce-and-shadow-lord-lasted-so-long?p=1400653#post1400653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And this kind of long long war has a common point: they rarely strike the very core of both sides<br /> <br /> We never hear of any really powerful, named elders were killed by lupines. Velya, Yoark, and so on. These 4th and 5th gen elders are still around (or killed by others, not lupines at least). Needless to say Eldest himself (In fact in the whole WoD we never hear of any named methseulah are killed by lupines). Maybe they slaughtered a lot but we didn't know<br /> Of course no named <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">legendary or elder </span></span></span>Shadow Lords were killed by vampires, too. Tzimisce didn't really eliminate them<br /> <br /> From this perspective, history of Set seems to be more suitable, he made all supernaturals of Egypt suck very, very hard thousands of years ago, letting Silent Striders leave home, ghouling all Kinfolk of Bubasti, etc. And they all happened after hunderds of years' war<br /> <b>Set is much younger than Tzimisce</b>, well</div> </div> </div> </div>We don't know who is &quot;older&quot; between Tzimisce and Set...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T10:02:12-07:00","id":1400768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400622-why-the-war-between-tzimisce-and-shadow-lord-lasted-so-long#post1400622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is, well, very strange that one side didn't do something really badass to crush down the other...</div> </div> </div> </div>Somehow I wrote a huge post but the power went out and now I'm kind of pissed off, so I'll keep it brief...<br /> <br /> I think that their war was more akin to a &quot;turf war&quot; than a real war. They intensively inhabited the same area, but that's it.<br /> Lords had the forests and peaks, Tzimisce had cities, castles and sometime peaks too.<br /> But the area they inhabited wasn't some secluded place or an isle, was basically the gate that separate central europe from eastern europe.<br /> <br /> This means that Tzimisce had other issues. They were meant to be the &quot;royal&quot; Clan in their land (the average Ventrue can be a noble, Tzimisce in DA e before thought themselves a step higher) and to keep the power on the kine they really couldn't devote their time to spar with the wolves. Stay in the cities, maybe let the humans build more cities and then relocate to the new one.<br /> Let some lesser-breed Kindred (like Nosferatu or Gangrel) or those crazy Kolduns roam the forests, they'll keep the wolves busy and away from the cities and with some luck will get killed as well.<br /> But the imperative is to control the cities.<br /> <br /> And the Lords have other issues too. Thanks to Kupala and other beings, the spiritual landscape of Dacia/Transylvania is nothing to scoff at. They can't just devote all their times to exterminate bloodsuckers. And why they should? It's a well-known fact that two or more vampires in the same room will try to off each other after some time, unless they find some bigger enemy that unites them. So if the Lords starts an all-out war, the vampires will fight side-to-side instead than trying to kill each other... (exactly what happened in the Chicago War)... and the Lords are more thoughtful than that.<br /> They pick their battles.<br /> Kill the vampires that roam the wild areas or those that encroach your sept's interests. Let the other think they are safe in the cities, this will keep all of them together and they will keep killing each other.<br /> <br /> Of course this also mean that can exist some unspoken agreements like &quot;we stay here, you stay there and when we pass each other we both pretend to look the other way&quot;, and this is also why the Lords got their reputation of deceitful untrustworthy backstabbers. &quot;After all&quot; the other Garou reason &quot;the leeches are just behind the next hill, why they don't assault them night after night?&quot;<br /> Because probably they and the Tzimisce will end up both destroyed by the conflict and some other group (the Silver Fang and Ventrue, for example) will just march in the lands taking their due and silencing the last surviving members that dare to speak aloud.<br /> <br /> But even without going with the full-strategic approach they were just <b>scared </b>of each other.<br /> Tzims know Lupines are strong, hunt in packs and have weird powers the Tzimisce couldn't understand or replicate. And those that replicated them sometime would end from the &quot;weird&quot; to the &quot;completely nuts&quot; (how else can you describe a Tzimisce that lives in secluded areas, at direct contact with... earth? Water? Wind? Whatever she's studying? Kolduns were strong and useful if they survived, but not every Tzim would go for that, not even for those powers).<br /> If you want to kill the a whole Sept you must march an army of reventants, Vohzd and Slachtza into the forest. You know that most of them will not return and you must hope they are enough to kill every werewolf in that cave you luckily found. And that's because you, the Elder or the Voivode, will certainly not march with them toward certain doom. Of course, you may send some Childer, the expendable ones.<br /> Then what? Your forces will be severely depleted, and you'll be weakened toward other vampires and voivodes.<br /> And that doesn't even take into account that you may not have killed all the werewolves, and that may call other wolves from outside to make an example of the weakened you.<br /> <br /> On the other side, the Lord know that the older vampires are so strong that you need whole packs to go toe-to-toe with one, that they have whole broods of younger, weaker, leeches near them and that they have weird flesh-shaping power they can't understand and that maybe only the Wyrm can replicate. They may have some spies (mainly Kinfolk) trying to spy on them, but generally steer away from cities.<br /> If you want to kill the Voivode, you must assault his castle, where all those horrors dwell. And even if you kill all the horrors, all the weird humans that doesn't scream running away but try to stab you with a spear, all those lesser leeches that somehow seems increasingly armed with silver the more older they become, you still need to go after the Big Bad. How many will survive such assault?<br /> Then what? Your forces will be severely depleted, and your sept (and maybe the other ones) will be so weakened that Wyrm minions (the real ones, not the unknowing ones) will find much easier to make Caerns fall one after the other.<br /> And that doesn't even take into account that you may not have killed all the leeches, and that the surviving ones may follow your surviving warriors, find the caerns or (even worse) your Kinfolk, your family and exterminate, maim or enslave them. This means that in one hundred year, that vampire will still be around, and there will not be any new Lord taking your place, while you died in that glorious assault or some years after that trying to defend your Caern from some Fomori.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, they were just scared of each other.<br /> Not because the other was more scary than them, but because the other side was strong enough to fatally cripple them and make them a target for more problematic foes.<br /> <br /> The relationship between Tzimisce and Shadow Lords is just that:<br /> &quot;You stay on your side of the fence, while I'll stay on mine... and try to move the fence the moment you look away. And in the meantime I'll kill all your friends that pass near my home.&quot;<br /> &quot;Gladly, I'll do the same&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/250518/Dark-Shores-Lineages--of-the-Great-Lakes\" target=\"_blank\">VTM: Dark Shores: Lineages of the Great Lakes</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/264262/Fingers-of-the-Eldest-Bogatyri\" target=\"_blank\">VTM: Fingers of the Eldest: Bogatyri</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/295115/Forgotten-Alliances\" target=\"_blank\">WTA: Forgotten Alliances</a>","edited":{"userid":24483,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24483-salamander","user":"SalamanDer","date":".  typos 07-04-2020, 01:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24483-salamander","name":"SalamanDer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24483_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T11:06:26-07:00","id":1400784,"title":"","content":"I think people overestimate the size of a &quot;war&quot; to be honest.<br /> <br /> There's going to be, what, 200 Lupines in all of the future country of Romania?<br /> <br /> Versus, maybe, 200 Voivoides?<br /> <br /> What qualifies as a &quot;War&quot; is going to be a different image than people imagine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T11:50:49-07:00","id":1400796,"title":"","content":"As noted above, each of these factions have one or more extremely powerful entities at their &quot;centre;&quot; the Shadow Lords have their totem Grandfather Thunder, and many other powerful Spirits; the Tzimisce have the Eldest and Kupala, along with wily and powerful Methuselahs. Completely toppling a faction, &quot;cutting the head off the snake,&quot; is an extremely difficult proposition in either case. And so long as that is not achieved, it is likely that some members of either side will manage to survive, regroup, and &quot;fight another night.&quot;<br /> <br /> And again, as noted above, even if both factions see the other as one of their chief rivals, it is rarely the case that they can gather their combined might all at once and commit it to the destruction of any particular 'nemesis.' Both groups have problems with in-fighting to varying degrees; both groups have other dangerous enemies who could take advantage if they over-extend themselves. And both groups often lack a comprehensive understanding of the other that would make such a strategic surgical strike possible; how much do the Shadow Lords know about the Antediluvians and Generation, how much do the Tzimisce know about Garou pacts with the Spirits?<br /> <br /> Things absolutely could go another way, dependent on conditions, but that's largely up to Storyteller fiat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T12:11:13-07:00","id":1400804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400622-why-the-war-between-tzimisce-and-shadow-lord-lasted-so-long?p=1400784#post1400784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think people overestimate the size of a &quot;war&quot; to be honest.<br /> <br /> There's going to be, what, 200 Lupines in all of the future country of Romania?<br /> <br /> Versus, maybe, 200 Voivoides?<br /> <br /> What qualifies as a &quot;War&quot; is going to be a different image than people imagine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fun fact, once we were playing DA TbN and a player asked me to explain how the hell worked this war if they were still at it after centuries.<br /> I said that they were going at it like the gang wars of GTA San Andreas. He nodded and started writing things down.<br /> Then, the chronicle totally derailed in a low-attrition war against the Lords for developing a contested area.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/250518/Dark-Shores-Lineages--of-the-Great-Lakes\" target=\"_blank\">VTM: Dark Shores: Lineages of the Great Lakes</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/264262/Fingers-of-the-Eldest-Bogatyri\" target=\"_blank\">VTM: Fingers of the Eldest: Bogatyri</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/295115/Forgotten-Alliances\" target=\"_blank\">WTA: Forgotten Alliances</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24483-salamander","name":"SalamanDer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24483_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T12:22:47-07:00","id":1400809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SalamanDer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400622-why-the-war-between-tzimisce-and-shadow-lord-lasted-so-long?p=1400804#post1400804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I said that they were going at it like the gang wars of GTA San Andreas. He nodded and started writing things down.<br /> Then, the chronicle totally derailed in a low-attrition war against the Lords for developing a contested area.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most fightings are just street-level gang wars, of course<br /> <br /> But if you want to strike elders or even methuselahs, things will be much more complex. Especially for methuselahs, your war may last centuries of years, and could be so epic and great that can be written in Silver Record, just like slaying Zmei<br /> <br /> For elders, see Vladimir Rustovich, he is a signature firstly appeared in a Werewolf book and was surely killed by lupines","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 07-03-2020, 03:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T12:23:21-07:00","id":1400811,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Vladimir_Rustovich#cite_note-0\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Vl...ch#cite_note-0</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T12:27:41-07:00","id":1400812,"title":"","content":"The werevolves of old did things like imprisoning Kupala and the Talons of the Wyrm and one of tyhose critters forced an Antediluvian into a stalemate at the very least. So yes the Shadow Lords have the potential power to compete with the Tzimisce. It's just that all out non stop war would possibly bring both of them to extinction falling prey to other enemies (admittedly, given how vampires and the Tzimisce in particular work they are probably better suited for attrition war but that not taking curses and the like into account).<br /> So they have their territories and frequently fight each others, sometimes someone starts a war but things are stopped when they come close to the &quot;nuclear option&quot;. Uneasy stalemates and armistices ensue and after a generation or two the cycle starts again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T14:54:17-07:00","id":1400828,"title":"","content":"Surprised nobody mentioned the Danislav so far (that I've seen). <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Danislavs\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Danislavs</a><br /> <br /> They were a major byproduct of the Tzimisce / Shadow Lord War, Revenants created by Voivode Count Florescu from captured Shadow Lord Kinfolk.<br /> <br /> Like Rustovich's whole existence, they are an important sign of the ongoing war.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T20:31:24-07:00","id":1400891,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind, what constitutes A war versus SEVERAL wars depends a lot on historians. Conflicts like the Hundred Year's War (which lasted longer than a hundred years) were only retroactively named such.<br /> <br /> Also, whether they actually see it as a war or a hunting expedition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-04T01:26:48-07:00","id":1400913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1400622-why-the-war-between-tzimisce-and-shadow-lord-lasted-so-long?p=1400784#post1400784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think people overestimate the size of a &quot;war&quot; to be honest.<br /> <br /> There's going to be, what, 200 Lupines in all of the future country of Romania?<br /> <br /> Versus, maybe, 200 Voivoides?<br /> <br /> What qualifies as a &quot;War&quot; is going to be a different image than people imagine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I always imagined it to be more of a cold war, with occasional assaults on a voivode's castle or a pack's sept, as opposed to the hundred or so participants on either side actually marshalling armies and fighting. And given both the Tzimisce and Shadow Lords tend to be more &quot;ruler types&quot; than &quot;soldier types&quot;, I picture the majority of the &quot;fighting&quot; to be through proxies and such. Again, more like a cold war with breaks for real battles. I don't see a sustainable (for either side) war lasting since prehistory being a thing of constant, or even semi-frequent fighting. There's just not enough garou or kindred for that type of thing to last long.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}